{"timestamp": "2026-07-20T16:43:39.056977", "user_message": "How do u make ice-cream", "final_answer": "An easy no-churn ice cream uses 2 cups of cold heavy cream, one 14-ounce can of sweetened condensed milk, 2 teaspoons of vanilla, and a small pinch of salt. Whip the cream to stiff peaks, gently fold in the other ingredients, cover it, and freeze it for at least 6 hours. Add fruit, chocolate, or cookies before freezing if you want a flavor mix-in.", "route": "general_conversation", "planner_used": "deterministic_fast_path", "planner_validated": true, "llm_synthesis_used": false, "critic_passed": true, "memory_found": false, "response_time": 0.0}
