{"timestamp": "2026-07-24T09:44:46.994296", "user_message": "Solve 3(2x - 5) = 27. State x and show the essential steps.", "final_answer": "To solve the equation \\(3(2x - 5) = 27\\), follow these steps:\n\n1. Distribute the 3 on the left side of the equation:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 2x - 3 \\cdot 5 = 27\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   6x - 15 = 27\n   \\]\n\n2. Add 15 to both sides of the equation to isolate the term with \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   6x - 15 + 15 = 27 + 15\n   \\]\n   This simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   6x = 42\n   \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by 6 to solve for \\(x\\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{42}{6}\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the fraction gives:\n   \\[\n   x = 7\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the solution is \\(x = 7\\).", "route": "general_conversation", "planner_used": "deterministic_fast_path", "planner_validated": true, "llm_synthesis_used": true, "critic_passed": true, "memory_found": false, "response_time": 16.65}
