{"timestamp": "2026-08-18T12:26:45.356243", "user_message": "Explain how stars form in three clear sentences.", "final_answer": "Stars form from clouds of gas and dust in space, known as molecular clouds. Gravity pulls material together, causing the cloud to collapse and heat up, forming a protostar. When the core temperature is high enough, nuclear fusion begins, marking the birth of a star.  \n**Conclusion:** Star formation is a gravitational collapse process driven by nuclear fusion in dense interstellar clouds.", "route": "general_conversation", "planner_used": "deterministic_fast_path", "planner_validated": true, "llm_synthesis_used": true, "critic_passed": true, "memory_found": false, "response_time": 1.28}
