{"timestamp": "2026-09-02T00:38:00.170650", "user_message": "What makes a good friendship feel trustworthy?", "final_answer": "That usually comes down to showing up when you need them most and keeping your word even when it's hard. Trust isn't built on grand gestures or perfect silence; it's the quiet reliability of someone who shows up, listens without judgment, and stands by their promises like a steady anchor in a storm. It feels safe because they know they can rely on that person to handle things for them, even if they're not always around.\n\nWhat makes you feel most secure when you're with someone new?", "route": "general_conversation", "planner_used": "deterministic_fast_path", "planner_validated": true, "llm_synthesis_used": true, "critic_passed": true, "memory_found": false, "response_time": 2.96}
{"timestamp": "2026-09-02T00:38:39.345150", "user_message": "Give me one everyday example of that trust.", "final_answer": "That trust usually shows up in the small, quiet moments when you're both stressed and you just need someone to lean on without trying to fix everything right away. Imagine you've been working late for hours and your phone buzzes with a message from a friend who hasn't heard from you all day; instead of rushing to send a long explanation or demanding an update, they simply reply with a simple, warm check-in like, \"Hey, how are you really doing?\" That kind of presence\u2014being there just to listen and hold space for them while they figure out their own next steps\u2014is what makes that trust feel real and safe.", "route": "general_conversation", "planner_used": "deterministic_fast_path", "planner_validated": true, "llm_synthesis_used": true, "critic_passed": true, "memory_found": false, "response_time": 3.19}
